        "content": "<p>V0ldek opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14968\">PR #14968</a> from <code>V0ldek:patch-1</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The filter for GC keywords was ending the entire test run in <code>/tests/wast.rs</code>. It's a one line bug where a <code>return</code> should be <code>continue</code>. It looks to be an inadvertent regression from #14245 where a closure was inlined into <code>main</code> and the <code>return</code> now concerns the entire suite and not just the single trial.</p>\n<p>To verify, I ran the command that is used in the CI run for GC Zeal where these filters are used and confirmed it returns zero trials. With this change it returns 300.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">RUSTFLAGS</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"--cfg gc_zeal\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WASMTIME_TEST_GC_KEYWORDS</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"gc drc any eq struct array i31 extern exn ref rec\"</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">list</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Linked: <a href=\"#narrow/channel/206238-general/topic/Spurious.20return.20in.20tests.2Fwast.2Ers/with/634475952\">#general &gt; Spurious return in tests/wast.rs</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
